    <!-- PROJECTS -->
    <section id="projects">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="section-label reveal">Work</p>
        <h2 class="section-title reveal">Products in production</h2>
        <div class="section-line reveal"></div>
        <p
          class="reveal"
          style="
            color: var(--muted);
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            max-width: 620px;
            margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
          "
        >
          Three builds that are live and carrying real users right now, with the
          decision behind each one and the number it produced.
        </p>
        <div class="projects-grid">
          <div class="project-card reveal">
            <div class="project-head">
              <div>
                <h3 class="project-name">Abraj</h3>
                <p class="project-number">01 &mdash; Live on Google Play</p>
              </div>
              <span class="stat-chip highlight">450,000+ downloads</span>
            </div>
            <div class="project-line">
              <span class="project-line-label">Problem</span>
              <p>A product with hundreds of thousands of installs had no user accounts and no wallet. Every install was an anonymous stranger the business could never reach again, and there was no way to send one user a message meant for them.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-line">
              <span class="project-line-label">My call</span>
              <p>I did not rebuild it. I layered accounts, wallets, authentication and an AI feature onto the live app, and registered every user &mdash; anonymous ones included &mdash; into notification topics, so an anonymous user can be reached today and keeps the same identity the moment they sign in with Google.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-line result">
              <span class="project-line-label">Result</span>
              <p>450,000+ downloads, top 3 in its category, 4.7&#9733; from 2,995 ratings, and ~3,000 people opening it every day.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-stats">
                <span class="stat-chip highlight">450,000+ downloads</span>
                <span class="stat-chip">4.7&#9733; / 2,995 ratings</span>
                <span class="stat-chip">~3,000 daily users</span>
                <span class="stat-chip">Top 3 in category</span>
            </div>
            <div class="project-tech">
                <span class="tech-tag">Flutter</span>
                <span class="tech-tag">Firebase</span>
                <span class="tech-tag">Push Notifications</span>
                <span class="tech-tag">AI</span>
                <span class="tech-tag">Full Stack</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="project-card reveal">
            <div class="project-head">
              <div>
                <h3 class="project-name">Yara Store &mdash; Inventory &amp; Expense System</h3>
                <p class="project-number">02 &mdash; Retail, still running</p>
              </div>
              <span class="stat-chip highlight">0 manual errors</span>
            </div>
            <div class="project-line">
              <span class="project-line-label">Problem</span>
              <p>The owner wrote every sale and expense on paper, then re-typed the day into Excel at night. Asking &ldquo;what am I about to run out of?&rdquo; meant flipping through pages, and every re-typing introduced errors that turned into real stock gaps.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-line">
              <span class="project-line-label">My call</span>
              <p>I cut the typing out entirely: scan the QR at the point of sale and the books write themselves. Then I put analytics on top &mdash; busiest days, top sellers, and basket analysis that suggests product C to anyone buying A and B.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-line result">
              <span class="project-line-label">Result</span>
              <p>Manual re-entry errors dropped to zero, a sale now takes under a second instead of a paper-then-Excel round trip, and the owner is still running his shop on it every day.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-stats">
                <span class="stat-chip highlight">0 re-entry errors</span>
                <span class="stat-chip">Under 1s per sale</span>
                <span class="stat-chip">In daily use today</span>
                <span class="stat-chip">Sales analytics</span>
            </div>
            <div class="project-tech">
                <span class="tech-tag">Flutter</span>
                <span class="tech-tag">Laravel</span>
                <span class="tech-tag">MySQL</span>
                <span class="tech-tag">QR Scanning</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="project-card reveal">
            <div class="project-head">
              <div>
                <h3 class="project-name">Supermarket POS &mdash; Checkout System</h3>
                <p class="project-number">03 &mdash; Shipped fast</p>
              </div>
              <span class="stat-chip highlight">Under 2 weeks</span>
            </div>
            <div class="project-line">
              <span class="project-line-label">Problem</span>
              <p>A single-branch supermarket needed a working till, and needed it soon. A months-long custom build or an enterprise POS contract would both have cost more than the problem was worth.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-line">
              <span class="project-line-label">My call</span>
              <p>I reused a proven base from a similar build instead of starting from zero, and held the scope to one branch and the checkout flow only &mdash; no features that would not earn their build time.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-line result">
              <span class="project-line-label">Result</span>
              <p>Delivered and running in under 2 weeks, handling 20&ndash;40 invoices a day.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="project-stats">
                <span class="stat-chip highlight">Shipped in under 2 weeks</span>
                <span class="stat-chip">20&ndash;40 invoices/day</span>
                <span class="stat-chip">Single branch</span>
            </div>
            <div class="project-tech">
                <span class="tech-tag">Flutter</span>
                <span class="tech-tag">Laravel</span>
                <span class="tech-tag">MySQL</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

